--TEST--
an attribute's name is coloured as a decorator, at its declaration and at each use — a use carries `defaultLibrary` for a `Core` attribute and nothing for a program's own declaration — a declared field is a property, as the key that sets it is, and the payload is coloured as the expressions it holds, `rule:attributes/attach-sites-and-forms`
--FILE--
<?nvs
attribute Tagged on method { tag: string }

class Blog
{
    #[Core\Route(path: "/", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Tagged(tag: "home")]
    public static function index(): string
    {
        return "hello";
    }

    repeatable attribute Cached on method { seconds: int }
}
--REQUEST--
semanticTokens types=decorator,type,enum,enumMember,property
--EXPECT--
2:11+6 decorator
2:30+3 property
6:7+10 decorator defaultLibrary
6:18+4 property
6:29+6 property
6:37+16 enum defaultLibrary
6:55+3 enumMember
7:7+6 decorator
7:14+3 property
13:26+6 decorator
13:45+7 property
